# Installed, not written here.
node_modules/

# Built by `npm run build`, from web/. Nothing in it is a source file.
dist/

# A self-signed certificate and its private key, made on this machine for testing on a phone.
# `npm run dev:lan` generates a fresh pair; they are never the same twice and never shared.
dev-certs/

# PairDrop's source, kept locally to read from. It is somebody else's project under its own
# licence and has no business in this repository, and nothing here is derived from the code.
reference/

# Notes written while working out what to build: a teardown of another project's architecture
# and protocol, a catalogue of its defects, and a survey of the alternatives. Useful, and not
# ours to publish - a list of a live project's security gaps, cross-referenced to file and line,
# is something you send to the people who maintain it, not something you post under your own
# name. Kept on disk; only the publishing stops.
docs/01-pairdrop-architecture.md
docs/02-pairdrop-protocol-reference.md
docs/03-defects-and-limits.md
docs/04-competitive-landscape.md

# The working papers behind the design: the blueprint that argued for it and the roadmap that
# set its targets. They cite the notes above by finding number and make their case by pointing
# at another project throughout, so they belong with the notes rather than with the app. What is
# worth publishing from them is the protocol spec, which is written to stand on its own.
docs/05-gear-drop-blueprint.md
docs/07-roadmap-and-benchmarks.md

# Editor and tooling state that belongs to one machine.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# What operating systems leave behind.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local overrides. There are no secrets in this project, and this is how it stays that way.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Scratch output.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage/
.vercel

# A throwaway CDP probe used to drive Chrome on a device over adb. Not part of the app.
cdp-probe.mjs
